What is taken from chardetng 1.0.0:
  - single_byte.mbt: the single-byte candidates (LatinCandidate,
    NonLatinCasedCandidate, ArabicFrenchCandidate, CaselessCandidate,
    LogicalCandidate, VisualCandidate) and their constants, ported from
    src/lib.rs, and SingleByteData with its classification and pair scoring,
    ported from src/data.rs. The punctuation counts of the Hebrew candidates
    are left out until the final guess that reads them is ported.
  - detector.mbt: how EncodingDetector feeds candidates (skipping leading
    ASCII, keeping two bytes of context, treating the end of the stream as a
    space) and how find_score reports a score without a top-level domain,
    ported from src/lib.rs. The CJK and ISO-2022-JP candidates and the
    guess are not ported yet.
  - single_byte_data.mbt: the byte classification and character-pair score
    tables, written by tools/gen_data.py from src/data.rs without changes.
    src/data.rs states: "Any copyright is dedicated to the Public Domain.
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
  - The expected scores in golden_data_test.mbt, produced by running
    chardetng 1.0.0 (tools/golden).

Tatoeba
  https://tatoeba.org
  Sentences licensed under CC BY 2.0 FR
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/).

  tools/corpus.tsv holds sentences from the Tatoeba per-language exports,
  each row with the Tatoeba ids of its sentences; tools/gen_corpus.py
  describes how they were chosen and the changes made to some rows
  (Romanian cedillas, Vietnamese tone marks for windows-1258, Hebrew in
  reverse order). golden_data_test.mbt contains these sentences encoded in
  UTF-8 and single-byte encodings.

Tools
  tools/golden builds against the crates chardetng 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT)
  and encoding_rs 0.8.42 ((Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause), with the
  versions of their dependencies pinned in tools/golden/Cargo.lock. They are
  used to produce test data and are not part of the MoonBit module.
